  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $F(x)=e^{x}, G(x)=e^{-x}$ $\\therefore \\quad\r\nH(x)=G(F(x))$ $\\begin{aligned} &=G\\left(e^{x}\\right) \\\\ &=e^{-e^{x}} \\\\ \\frac{d H}{d x} &=e^{-e^{x}} \\cdot\\left(-e^{x}\\right) \\\\ &=-e^{x} e^{-e^{x}} \\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\left.\\therefore \\quad \\frac{d H}{d x}\\right|_{x=0}=-e^{0} \\cdot e^{-e^{0}}$\r\n$=-1 . e^{-1}$\r\n$=-e^{-1}$\r\n$=\\frac{-1}{e}$",
    "image": null
  },
